The ONNX graph is an exported representation; its exact bytes and frontend
contract are declared in configs/uid-ecapa-binding.json. The upstream model
card declares Apache-2.0. SpeechBrain-LICENSE contains the upstream license.

Modification: AIII retrained the final projection (weight and bias) of this
model; all other weights are the upstream checkpoint's. The modified ONNX graph
has SHA-256 46aef1e6f483a2033eb88344b3d0d09b21d177c15cf45e45b0451d207de1fc99.
The upstream attribution and Apache-2.0 license above are retained.

Projection training data: the dev-other partition of "LibriSpeech ASR corpus"
(OpenSLR SLR12) by Vassil Panayotov with the assistance of Daniel Povey,
derived from read audiobooks from the LibriVox project.
Source: https://www.openslr.org/12
License: CC BY 4.0, https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/
Changes: AIII built clean-preservation and separation-artifact training pairs
from these recordings; the separated audio is output of the plugin's MossFormer2
separator (Apache-2.0, noticed separately). No endorsement by the licensor is
implied.

Frontend reference: SpeechBrain 1.1.1 Fbank and sentence-mean normalization.
Source: https://github.com/speechbrain/speechbrain/tree/v1.1.1
Our native frontend implements that feature contract without Python at runtime.

PocketFFT is statically incorporated into the native feature transform.
